---
import Plate from "./Plate.astro";
---
<section class="section feature" aria-labelledby="feature-h">
  <div class="grid">
    <h2 id="feature-h" class="c-head" data-reveal>675 students,<br />one honest question</h2>
    <p class="c-right justify feature__text" data-scramble>
      Can a school act on an early-warning prediction with the data it actually has at
      the time? With an anonymised Mathematics cohort of 675 students, the answer for
      many published models was no. IC-FS keeps the prediction honest.
    </p>
    <div class="c-full crop feature__frame" data-parallax>
      <div class="feature__clip">
        <div data-parallax-inner><Plate kind="cohort" id="feature" alt="675 dots, one per student in the cohort; the last columns are marked as data not yet available at prediction time" /></div>
      </div>
      <a class="btn btn--outline feature__btn" href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.eswa.2026.134262" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read in ESWA</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .feature__text { margin-top: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem; }
  .feature__frame { position: relative; }
  .feature__clip { overflow: hidden; aspect-ratio: 16 / 7; }
  .feature__clip > div { height: 116%; margin-top: -8%; }
  .feature__clip :global(.plate) { height: 100%; }
  .feature__btn { position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: 2.5rem; translate: -50% 0; color: #fff; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.15); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .feature__clip { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; } }
</style>
